! THE LOJBAN MOO IS DEAD

As Robin Lee Powell if you want details, but the short version is
that it was always super-slow and the popularity wasn't enough to
justify the time to do a complete rewrite.

{maketoc}

! Introduction

There is now a Lojban [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/MOO|MOO]; that is, a multi user virtual environment, kind of like the old text adventure games.  One of the things we're trying to use it for is ((xartum)).  To that end, we need people to come visit and {ALINK(aname=>prayer)}pray{ALINK} for or {ALINK(aname=>build,pagename=>Lojban MOO Lojban Commands)}build{ALINK} the things they want!

!! How To Get Help

In Lojban, you can get a list of available commands at ((Lojban MOO Lojban Commands)).

If you're in English, you can use the in-MOO help system by typing "help".

In Lojban, you can use "sidju", but only one or two pages are translated.  You can use "mulsidju" to access the English help (although as of 19 July 2006, that is very slow).

Help can often be gotten on ((Lojban IRC)).

If you're really stuck, you can [mailto:rlpowell@digitalkingdom.org|mail the MOO admin].

For general information on MOOs and MUDs and so on, see [http://www.mudconnect.com/mudfaq/|The MUD FAQ] or [http://www.moo.mud.org/moo-faq/|The MOO FAQ].  In particular, [http://www.mudconnect.com/mudfaq/mudfaq-p1.html#q5|How Do I Connect To A MUD], [http://www.mudconnect.com/mudfaq/mudfaq-p1.html#q7|Now that I'm connected, what do I do?], [http://www.mudconnect.com/mudfaq/mudfaq-p1.html#q14|What common commands are used on MUDs?], [http://www.mudconnect.com/mudfaq/mudfaq-p2.html#q1|What is a client?] and [http://www.mudconnect.com/mudfaq/mudfaq-p2.html#q5|What different clients are avialable?].

